insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1eb1749d-8371-5de5-ad03-ae0c02f79bdc', 'rg3-text-structure-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Soccer and Futsal$q$, $q$Soccer is played all over the world. Futsal is a smaller kind of soccer that is played indoors. The two games share many rules, but they also have some big differences.

Heading: The Same Goal

In both games, players try to kick a ball into the other team's net. Players may not touch the ball with their hands, except for the goalkeeper. Both games reward good passing and teamwork.

Heading: The Field and the Ball

Soccer is played outside on a large grass field. Futsal, on the other hand, is played on a hard court, often inside a gym. A futsal ball is smaller than a soccer ball, and its inside is filled with soft padding. Because of this, it does not bounce as much.

Heading: The Teams

A soccer team has eleven players on the field. A futsal team has only five. With fewer players and a smaller space, futsal players touch the ball much more often.

Sidebar, Coach's Tip: Many young players practice futsal in winter to sharpen their footwork for soccer in spring.

Picture caption: Two futsal players chase a ball across a shiny gym floor.$q$, 'draft')
